In article <9262@star.cs.vu.nl> lbkruij@cs.vu.nl (Kruijswijk Lucas B) writes:

>I don't know how but it would be fun when you really can
>fight with magic. Isn't it a little bit strange that a wizard has no magic
>to protect himself against a normal weapon? I can't imagine that Gandalf was
>very strong person dressed as a knight.

Unless, of course, he wished so. In any case, I would like to play a wizard
that can manage in the dungeon without having to worry about finding armor
and weapons, perhaps a silver dagger not included.

A low level wizard should be able to use some minor protection spells like
cloaking or stealth and some attacking spells like magic missile. When he/she
rises in rank, he/she would get more powerful spells. Perhaps they should
be given and be permanent? (A wizard could continue to use normal spellbooks
as before.)

ANOTHER THING that I've been thinking of is the cursed/non cursed/blessed
objects. I think the effects of objects when they are cursed vs. blessed
is too different. Of course, some difference in their effects is good, but
NO object should have almost opposite effects when cursed vs. blessed. That
just has the undesired effect of making the game more random. Random in 
a sense that the game doesn't reward a player that knows his business..

